!
! One party's obligation on one due date, in Trebago (handfast_rules.h
! HR4), one obligation per row: floor(amount / obligors), plus one minor
! unit for the first amount mod obligors parties (pos 1..obligors), so the
! parts sum to the amount exactly. Trebago is exact and has no floor, so
! q = floor(amount / obligors) is counted three digits at a time from the
! top: each group the count of k = 1 to 999 with k * step * obligors <=
! what is left, which min(1, max(0, y - k * step * obligors + 1)) is for
! integers. q is at most amount, below 10^15, so the top group is 10^12.
! What is left at the end is the remainder, amount - q * obligors, and it
! gives the extra unit when pos <= it. ok is 0 for an amount outside
! 0..999999999999999, obligors outside 1..999 or pos outside
! 1..obligors, and the answer is divided by it: refused. share.sutra
! holds obligors to 9(2): past it the two disagree and it is held.
trebago obligation_share
  in  amount(n), obligors(n), pos(n)
  out share(n)
  var y(n), a(n), b(n), c(n), d(n), e(n), q(n), ok(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, amount(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, 999999999999999 - amount(i) + 1)) &
        * min(1, max(0, obligors(i))) * min(1, max(0, 999 - obligors(i) + 1)) &
        * min(1, max(0, pos(i))) * min(1, max(0, obligors(i) - pos(i) + 1))
  y(i) = amount(i) * ok(i)
  a(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, y(i) - k * 1000000000000 * obligors(i) + 1)))
  y(i) = y(i) - a(i) * 1000000000000 * obligors(i)
  b(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, y(i) - k * 1000000000 * obligors(i) + 1)))
  y(i) = y(i) - b(i) * 1000000000 * obligors(i)
  c(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, y(i) - k * 1000000 * obligors(i) + 1)))
  y(i) = y(i) - c(i) * 1000000 * obligors(i)
  d(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, y(i) - k * 1000 * obligors(i) + 1)))
  y(i) = y(i) - d(i) * 1000 * obligors(i)
  e(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, y(i) - k * obligors(i) + 1)))
  y(i) = y(i) - e(i) * obligors(i)
  q(i) = a(i) * 1000000000000 + b(i) * 1000000000 + c(i) * 1000000 + d(i) * 1000 + e(i)
  share(i) = (q(i) + min(1, max(0, y(i) - pos(i) + 1))) / ok(i)
end
